## Red r3 (2026-11-07) — step-made build tag

- Role base: `d456c90ba3c2ad616d16a3eec13ef0aaf78e54df`
- Status: DONE
- Scope: tests only. No workflow, Cloud Build, runbook, or script file changes.
- Task: the four push files (accounts, primary-advantage, storytime, workbooks) must
  escape the tag slice as `$${BUILD_ID:0:8}`, must not hold an unescaped
  `${BUILD_ID:0:8}`, and the deploy step must map `BUILD_ID=$BUILD_ID` in `env`.
  One new guard case rejects an invalid substitution in any push or traffic file.

### Changed cases

- W-11-primary, W-11-storytime, W-11-accounts, W-11-workbooks: each deploy step must
  hold `--tag=<prefix>-$${BUILD_ID:0:8}`, must not hold an unescaped
  `${BUILD_ID:0:8}`, and its env must hold exactly `BUILD_ID=$BUILD_ID`.
- W-15: same three checks for the storytime tag, then the rendered tag is 11
  characters and tag plus `storytime-app` is 24.
- F-17 (new, `cloudbuild-files.test.mjs`): all 16 push and traffic files
  (`files_checked=16`) must hold no unescaped `${...}` whose inner text is not
  `[A-Z_][A-Z0-9_]*`. The check uses the lookbehind `(?<!\$)\$\{([^}]*)\}` so an
  escaped `$${...}` is not a hit.
- Helper `pushAndTrafficFiles()` in `helpers/plan.mjs` lists the 10 push and 6
  traffic files under `FIXTURE_ROOT`.

